@api = http://localhost:5002
@receiver = http://localhost:5100

### What this sample exposes
GET {{api}}/

### Place an order - the order row and the outbox row are saved by one SaveChangesAsync
POST {{api}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "tenantId": "acme", "customerId": "cust-1", "total": 99.50 }

### What the receiver got
GET {{receiver}}/deliveries

### Summary: total vs distinct outbox ids
GET {{receiver}}/deliveries/summary

### The manual baseline script, for adopting an outbox table EF did not create
GET {{api}}/baseline-script

### Reset the receiver
DELETE {{receiver}}/deliveries
